```python
def memoize(func):
    cache = {}
    def wrapper(*args):
        if args not in cache:
            cache[args] = func(*args)
        return cache[args]
    wrapper.cache = cache
    return wrapper
```
`args` is already a tuple, which is hashable — so you can use it directly as a dict key.

The same pattern recording every input ever seen (without de-duplicating):
```python
def record(func):
    log = []
    def wrapper(*args):
        log.append(args)
        return func(*args)
    wrapper.log = log
    return wrapper
```
